### 2. Implementation: `MongoKnowledgeStore`

```java
package com.example.service;

import org.springframework.data.mongodb.core.MongoTemplate;
import org.springframework.data.mongodb.core.query.Criteria;
import org.springframework.data.mongodb.core.query.Query;

public class MongoKnowledgeStore implements KnowledgeStore {

    private final MongoTemplate mongoTemplate;
    private final String collectionName;

    public MongoKnowledgeStore(MongoTemplate mongoTemplate, String collectionName) {
        this.mongoTemplate = mongoTemplate;
        this.collectionName = collectionName;
    }

    @Override
    public String retrieveContext(String input) {
        Query query = new Query(Criteria.where("flowIdentifier").is(input));
        KnowledgeDoc doc = mongoTemplate.findOne(query, KnowledgeDoc.class, collectionName);
        if (doc == null) {
            // Fallback: treat input as raw text and search content field (optional)
            query = new Query(Criteria.where("content").regex(input, "i")); // Case-insensitive search
            doc = mongoTemplate.findOne(query, KnowledgeDoc.class, collectionName);
        }
        return doc != null ? doc.getContent() : "No context found for input: " + input;
    }

    public static class KnowledgeDoc {
        private String flowIdentifier;
        private String content;

        public String getFlowIdentifier() {
            return flowIdentifier;
        }

        public void setFlowIdentifier(String flowIdentifier) {
            this.flowIdentifier = flowIdentifier;
        }

        public String getContent() {
            return content;
        }

        public void setContent(String content) {
            this.content = content;
        }
    }
}
```

**Notes**:
- Searches by `flowIdentifier` first; if not found, falls back to a content search using regex (configurable behavior).
- Each instance is tied to a specific `collectionName`, allowing team-specific knowledge stores.

